The discussion centered on writing a methods appendix for a report on soil management adaptation practices. James provided an introductory section citing estimates for various agricultural practices from \citet{moran2013assessing} and shared relevant R code for calibrating adaptation models. I helped refine the text and suggested a concise description of both the calibration and the application of the adaptation model. I also provided LaTeX code for including the `mac-soil` figure, which illustrates the marginal adaptation cost curve. Subsequently, James expressed a need to include two additional figures related to variability in agricultural losses due to extreme events, which led to a compact rewrite of the variability section and the preparation of LaTeX code for displaying these results.
